<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11290" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπᾰλέξ-ω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ward off from,</i> c. acc. rei et gen. pers., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ δέ κεν ἄλλον σεῦ ἀπαλεξήσαιμι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.371
				</span></i>
			: c. dat. pers., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεὺς . . μοι
				ἀπαλέξαι γάμον</span>
			<i>may</i> he <i>avert</i> it <i>from</i> me, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1053
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc. pers.
			et gen. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ὥς τιν᾽ ἔμελλεν ἀπαλεξήσειν
					κακότητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.364
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>defend oneself,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ταῦτ᾽ ἀπαλέξασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					166
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				303
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				829
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
